    "notes": "The web analytics process is a cycle, not a one-time project: define KPIs → implement tracking → create reports → analyse → produce insights and recommendations → implement changes → analyse the website again. The arrow points to \"Implement Tracking\" because this chapter is about that step. Every later step depends on it: if tracking is missing or wrong, every report, KPI and recommendation built on it will also be wrong. Analysts often say \"garbage in, garbage out\". In practice, implementing tracking means three things: (1) setting up the analytics tool (GA4) correctly, (2) installing tags on the website, usually through GTM, and (3) testing that the right data arrives.",
