    "notes": "This is the Google tag (gtag.js). Google used to call it the Global Site Tag; the code is the same. Line by line: the first script downloads the gtag.js library asynchronously (async means it does not block the page from loading). The second script creates window.dataLayer — a JavaScript array that stores events and commands — and defines gtag(), which simply pushes commands into dataLayer. gtag('js', new Date()) records the time the tag loaded. gtag('config', 'G-…') tells the library which GA4 data stream to send data to. The dataLayer you see here is the same dataLayer that Google Tag Manager uses, which is why the two tools work well together.",
