    "notes": "Destination = the Google product that receives data, such as a GA4 web data stream (G-…) or a Google Ads account (AW-…). Before: the GTM container (gtm.js) loaded, then the Google tag fired and downloaded a second library (gtag.js) for each tag ID. That extra download added delay and sometimes caused timing problems — for example, an event firing before the configuration had loaded. After (optimized container, October 2026): the container sends data directly to each destination using Destination tags, with settings applied once for the whole container. Benefits: faster pages, more reliable data collection and one place to manage settings and user access. Your GA4 Event tags, triggers and variables are not changed. The Conversion Linker tag (used by Google Ads) becomes unnecessary for optimized destinations because the destination tags take over its job — but check any destinations that are not yet optimized before removing it.",
