    "title": "What's New in Google Tag Manager: Consent Mode v2 and GTM's Consent Controls",
    "text": [
     "Privacy laws (e.g., GDPR in the EU) require websites to ask before storing cookies. Consent mode lets Google tags adjust their behaviour to the visitor's choice in the cookie banner (the CMP).",
     "Basic vs. advanced",
     "Basic: tags do not load until the visitor consents.",
     "Advanced: tags load with consent \"denied\" by default and send cookieless pings that Google uses for modelling.",
     "Recent GTM controls",
     "Consent mode override (Aug 2024): sets default consent to denied for chosen regions.",
     "Manage data transmission (2026): block or delay advertising requests until ad_storage is granted.",
     "Preview (2026): shows requests that were delayed for missing consent.",
     "Test both states: in Preview, click Accept and Reject on your banner and confirm what is sent each time. A tag that fires before the banner's choice is applied is a consent \"race condition\".",
     "Consent type | Controls",
     "analytics_storage | Cookies for analytics (e.g., GA4 visit duration)",
     "ad_storage | Cookies for advertising",
     "ad_user_data | Sending user data to Google for ads",
     "ad_personalization | Personalised advertising / remarketing"
    ],
    "notes": "Consent mode connects your cookie banner (Consent Management Platform, CMP) with Google tags. Basic consent mode: Google tags are blocked until the visitor accepts. Advanced consent mode: tags load immediately with consent set to \"denied\"; while denied they send cookieless pings, which Google uses to model (estimate) missing conversions and behaviour. Consent mode v2 (required by Google for EEA advertising since 2024) added two signals — ad_user_data and ad_personalization — to the original analytics_storage and ad_storage. GTM controls: the consent mode override (Aug 2024) sets default consent to denied for selected regions, overriding the site's own default code. In 2026, \"Manage data transmission\" can delay or fully block advertising requests until ad_storage is granted, and Preview shows which requests were delayed because consent was missing. A \"race condition\" happens when a tag fires before the banner's choice is applied — always test both Accept and Reject.",
